* Behavioral model of the LDO for whole_chip, the same ports as ldo.cir, its parameters fitted at tt 3.3 V 27 C into model_params.inc by helpers/bandgap_ldo_model.py and checked against the transistor design at the other corners by make models: an error amplifier (ld_gm into ld_r1 and ld_c1, the first pole) drives the gate node around vref + ld_off plus the follower's no-load overdrive, a square-law follower (ld_k) from vdd sources the output, a bleed ld_ib and the output MIM ld_cout load it (the second pole, gm over ld_cout), so the loop's DC gain, crossover and margin at no load are the transistor's and its large-signal swing follows the square law; quiescent current ld_iq; bias and bleed scale with vref (all bias comes from the bandgap), the follower needs vdd above vout, and the 50 mV tanh widths only smooth the switching for the solver; vg is not used and the supply path is not modelled, so the model has no PSRR.
.subckt ldo vout fb vref vg vdd vss
Bea vss g i = ld_gm * (v(vref,vss) + ld_off - v(fb,vss))
Bbias bias vss v = v(vref,vss) + ld_off + sqrt(ld_ib / ld_k)
Rg g bias {ld_r1}
Cg g vss {ld_c1}
Bpass vdd vout i = ld_k * pow(max(v(g,vout), 0), 2) * max(tanh(v(vdd,vout) / 0.05), 0)
Bbl vout vss i = ld_ib * min(max(v(vref,vss), 0) / bg_v0, 1) * max(tanh(v(vout,vss) / 0.05), 0)
Cout vout vss {ld_cout}
Bq vdd vss i = (ld_iq - ld_ib) * min(max(v(vref,vss), 0) / bg_v0, 1)
.ends ldo
